      "side": 1,
      "message": "I created the mutator, but it turned out that that on its own didn\u0027t result in the behaviour that we want because in non-HWASAN builds it resulted in the HWASAN runtime being installed to /system/lib64 instead of /system/lib64/bootstrap. What we really want in that case is for the HWASAN runtime not to be installed at all.\n\nIt turns out that the reason why it was being installed in non-HWASAN builds was that it was being added to LLNDK_LIBRARIES. Any libraries in LLNDK_LIBRARIES are installed by default even if nothing depends on them. So I also made a change to filter out HWASAN from LLNDK_LIBRARIES. If an explicit dependency on HWASAN is declared (or an implicit one via SANITIZE_TARGET), that should still result in the sanitizer runtime being installed because of build dependencies.\n\nThat also required that I change ld.config.txt to include %SANITIZER_RUNTIME_LIBRARIES% in shared_libs in one case in which we weren\u0027t including both sets of libraries.",
